estion/id #uuid "ba0cfb4d-b95f-53bb-bb85-4ea4d8bd37c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141537" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+10x+16.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 5x+16\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $16$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{5}^{2}+16\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2}+16\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+5{)}^{2}-9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141548/selection/9a1631500b560448e5d67823a9dbda906097ccb824bd7368a3c0c55f501a3e0e" :answer/id #uuid "f0ea9da7-e30e-5564-b1bd-8e95d6c4d81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+7{)}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141548/selection/be95f0a79903ac872cee90085153aca09aa5d4c40f99930b5276194b01a2bd0a" :answer/id #uuid "38979c67-6fae-57b4-b8c4-b837b0a5fea5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+7{)}^{2}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141548/selection/2008a57f05d2d23272efc16276068f481b016728bdff9a4f2e390b925c802802" :answer/id #uuid "d27e9383-c0a3-5a04-96bc-1652cf341228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+14{)}^{2}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141548/selection/d149916a40574b9b6250fe7fbb8b966c45f8da9f91bcd887ddc3360dafa4913b" :answer/id #uuid "93cd80f2-6d5e-53a5-9e9d-8dff371b24ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+14{)}^{2}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141548/selection/0b445430dccbd170c21